cartridge "SLITHER/AHOY! NOV 1985/2026"

' SLITHER
' A ColecoVision game based on "Slither", Ahoy! November 1985 (Commodore
' 64 BASIC type-in; the program and the disk do not name its author).
' Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by
' Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game: a snake slithers through the forty rooms of a castle and never
' stops. Steer it with the stick; it leaves its body behind it wherever it
' goes, and running into a wall or into its own trail costs a life. Each
' room hides as many treasures as the difficulty (1 to 5); eat them all to
' earn the room's bonus and go on to the next room. After room 40 comes a
' big bonus, extra lives, and the forty rooms again one difficulty higher.
'
' From the original (orig/slither.bas): the forty rooms, their names and
' their walls (the listing's wall lines); the snake never stops and never
' shrinks, its trail stays until it crashes; a crash wipes the whole trail
' and the snake starts again at the top left heading right, the treasures
' it has not eaten stay; difficulty 1-5 = treasures per room and the
' snake's colour (white, yellow, green, grey, magenta); twelve kinds of
' treasure, one kind per room (room n has kind n, rooms 12-40 kind 12)
' worth 10, 25, 50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 175, 200, 250, 300, 400; the room
' bonus is the next value (25 .. 500); treasures land on a random empty
' cell away from the right and bottom walls, never on the start; seven
' lives, at most nine; after room 40: the twelve values times the
' difficulty, difficulty + 1 (at most 5), that many more lives; a high score.
'
' Liberties: the rooms are scaled from the C64's 38 x 21 field to 26 x 19
' (every room checked open everywhere, as on the C64); the snake glides a
' pixel at a time, one cell every 6 frames, which crosses a room in about
' the time the C64 took; the stick is remembered until the next cell (the
' C64 read it once a step); pulling straight back is ignored (on the C64 it
' was an instant crash into the snake's own neck); the trail is drawn in
' joined pieces; the wipe after a crash sweeps down the room row by row; the
' walls change colour every room; the room name sits in the top wall; the
' score is kept in BCD (6 digits); no "play again" question, the title
' comes back instead; the colour flashing of the crash is left out
' (nothing flashes).
'
' Controls: controller 1 (or 2): the stick steers. On the title, left and
' right choose the difficulty, up and down START or CREDITS, a button
' starts.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects after;
' the title tune is played once. `set sprite count` is always given.

